# The deck talk, the Prologue's Scene 6 (#187). Played by the DeckTalk
# trigger (a StoryTrigger at the top of the hatch ramp) the first time you
# come up on deck after the lantern's soup (the flag warmed_lantern). The
# rain is easing. The captain is at the wheel, the lantern beside him, and
# they're mid-talk as you come up. Your side is the reply you pick.
#
# It ends with them sending you to bed: sleeping in your bunk now sails on
# through the night to the island (Bedside, the flag deck_talk).

~ start
set deck_talk
@rain 0.2 8.0
@place heron wheel
@place lantern beside_the_helm
@face heron lantern
@shot the_helm cut
@wait 0.6
lantern: Much better, isn't it?
heron: Yes. Much.
lantern: I was beginning to think I'd never feel warm again.
heron: Let's hope you don't make a habit of nearly putting yourself out.
@look lantern pleased
lantern: I'll try.
@place player by_the_helm
@face heron player
@shot the_three cut
@wait 0.6
heron: We've lost a little time, but we haven't lost our way.
@face heron the_chart
heron: We're still heading for the island.
@look lantern surprised
lantern: Oh! I do like that island.
@face heron lantern
heron: You've never been there.
@look lantern pleased
lantern: I like the look of it.
- (Look between them) -> the_last_mark

~ the_last_mark
@face heron player
heron: It's the last mark on the old chart. Whatever we're looking for, there's a good chance we'll find a clue there.
lantern: I wonder what it'll be like.
heron: Probably wet.
@look lantern surprised
lantern: Everything's wet!
@wait 0.8
heron: Get some sleep. We'll make land by morning.
@look lantern pleased
lantern: Sleep well! I'll keep a lookout.
@home lantern
@shot free
-> END
